 # Extra kernel config for this build.
#
# INTENTIONALLY EMPTY — do not add CONFIG_ lines here without checking the
# exported-symbol CRCs first.
#
# History: this file used to request CONFIG_TMPFS_XATTR=y (it was needed by a
# path-hiding LKM). That option changes the GKI image's exported symbol CRCs.
# The ROM flashes its own vendor modules (vendor_dlkm) built against the stock
# GKI image, so with the option enabled every one of them fails at load time
# with
#
#     disagrees about version of symbol ...
#
# and the device stops at the boot animation. It also silently poisons any
# module this CI builds: msm_drm.ko compiled against a TMPFS_XATTR kernel does
# not load on a ROM running the stock GKI image.
#
# The LTPO/ADFR work needs no extra kernel config at all — the patches touch
# oplus_adfr.c and the panel device tree only — so the kernel is left
# bit-identical to the ROM's own GKI configuration.
